  "Densities: one primary per alloy with source URLs; ranges recorded where sources disagree beyond rounding (research/ringblank-data-2026-09-19.md section 1). Cooksongold-derived values = 21.45 / relative factor and are marked derived.",
  "Ring size tables are generated from formulas (no supplier chart copied): US ID_mm = 0.8128*size + 11.63 (Wikipedia; cross-checked vs Rio Grande PDF within 0.06 mm for sizes 3-10); UK BS 6820:1987 circ = 37.5 + 1.25*index(A=0), half = +0.625; ISO 8653 / JIS S 4700 size = inner circumference mm; JCS gou ID_mm = 13.0 + (n-1)/3.",
  "The Japanese 'gou' system is JCS (Japan Custom Size), not JIS S 4700 (which is the ISO circumference number). Requirements wording should be corrected.",
  "Disputed UK M: BS 6820 formula gives 16.71 mm ID; retail charts show 16.51-16.92. Shipped value 16.71 with footnote.",
  "Gauge: B&S/AWG per ASTM B258 formula d_in = 0.005*92^((36-n)/39); matches Wikipedia table on all rows 0-30.",
  "Wide band: published rule is flat +0.5 mm when width > 4 mm (Rio Grande PDF; Orchid janetb 2021). No per-mm slope found; the '+0.5 x (width-4)' form in research section 4 is unsourced. Alternatives: +1/4 US size (iMakeJewelry per Orchid), +1/2 size (Orchid 2011).",
